m_map ([0:({"Rag",252,"<ArchWizard>","Current monster tune","Tue Jun 10 21:19:43 2003",4,1,"Here are some suggestions that might balance the mud.Remove the current overkill monsters (Celtron's dam-tune)More hitpoints for monstersMore physical resistances and less elemental resistancesWith these tunes some parties might want to get a mage fortheir party. Maybe even uptune bolts.Just some ideas, please comment :)-Rag",}),1:({"Celtron",1000,"<God>","skill/ability weapon finesse","Sun Jul 14 01:03:34 2002",1,0,"Uses DEX instead of STR when calculating damage etcetc",}),2:({"Celtron",1000,"<God>","wimpy","Wed Aug 21 12:16:54 2002",4,0,"something is wrong with it..",}),3:({"Walla",135,"<Apprentice Wizard>","who","Fri Jul 19 14:04:40 2002",3,1,"who command could be improved, as to understand who <guild>and cool stuff like thatjust my 2 <insert currency here>-walla",}),4:({"Gynter",202,"<Wizard>","new slot","Thu Aug  1 01:26:22 2002",4,1,"Was wondering if we couldn't make a new slot for eq?For lameass wizardcreated eq? (nonstat eq, eq not worth anything)Like headband,armband,tattoo,tshirt that kinda thingSo we could make some eq like Tattoo that says \"Gynter for worldleader\" etc :)And could make lameass trivias when we are bored and give the mortals some nonsuffeli eqthat they could use without compromising their current eq and lower their rate../gynt's lameass ideas <tm>",}),5:({"Balrog",140,"<Apprentice Wizard>","outworld monsters","Sat Jan 17 02:38:52 2004",5,0,"I have created a few monsters with nothing but descriptions to be usedfor the job/task nr. 48: outworld monsters.They're located here: /wizards/balrog/monsters/Have a look see. And whoever takes it on... good luck!- Balrog",}),6:({"Balrog",140,"<Apprentice Wizard>","grep","Tue Jan 20 14:29:17 2004",6,0,"I found a minor error in my grep.I tried fixing it on my version so I would just tell nalle to fix it..However, since it didnt really want to update grep for me (it kept givingthe same old reply even tho I had updated and changed the code dramatically).I thought someone else could fix it..The error shows itself in the manner that hits above 1000 rows are displayed with1 value too high on the row number... if a hit is found on 3640 for instance.You would have to use 3639p in the editor to see it.Thus.. it displays +1 in the row number... It should be easilly adjusted by Rag or Nalle.- Balrog",}),])
r_map ([0:({3,0,"Nalle",600,"who","<God>","Thu Nov 14 18:57:06 2002","I added some features to 'who'.",}),1:({4,0,"Devil",100,"new slot","<Apprentice Wizard>","Thu May  8 23:01:22 2003","Yeah that sould be nice, just do it :)?",}),2:({0,0,"Rag",252,"Current monster tune","<ArchWizard>","Tue Jun 10 21:23:11 2003","Oh, and downtune all melee damage. That might slow someplayers down just a bit.-Rag",}),])
